From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system: provision startup capabilities and gate guest
 hypercalls

Introduce the common startup policy source and explicit CLI selection. Freeze
before board initialization; bare startup remains zero. Restore upstream ARM
reserved-instruction decoding and ordinary other-target instruction paths when
guest-hypercall is absent, and do not install the x86 port region. User-only
translators keep a constant-off wrapper with no system-policy dependency.

This bounded first gate is not complete vanilla parity: the earlier series has
additional independently inventoried behavior changes still requiring off paths.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later AND MIT
Origin: new
